<article class="env-lemma" id="0154">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0154">Lemma <span data-tag="0154">13.12.3</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category. Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ 0 \ar[r] &  A^\bullet \ar[r] &  B^\bullet \ar[r] &  C^\bullet \ar[r] &  0 }  \]
</div>
  <p> be a short exact sequences of complexes. Assume this short exact sequence is termwise split. Let $(A^\bullet , B^\bullet , C^\bullet , \alpha , \beta , \delta )$ be the distinguished triangle of $K(\mathcal{A})$ associated to the sequence. The $\delta $-functor of Lemma <a href="/tag/0152" data-tag="0152">13.12.1</a> above maps the short exact sequences $0 \to A^\bullet \to B^\bullet \to C^\bullet \to 0$ to a triangle isomorphic to the distinguished triangle </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  (A^\bullet , B^\bullet , C^\bullet , \alpha , \beta , \delta ).  \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/014L" data-tag="014L">13.9.14</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>